      <title>2026 AMIE Annual Conference and Gala at Westin Hotel</title>
      <description><![CDATA[<div>  <img src="https://localist-images.azureedge.net/photos/53240039283260/huge/b21d8da97d4721aa1c486fc8522d999b01a05035.jpg" style="width: 100%;" />  <div style="font-size: 0.9em; color: #555;"><strong>Mon, 21 Sep 2026</strong></div>  <div><p>The 2026 AMIE Annual Conference and Gala hosted by Howard University will be held on Sunday, September 20th, through Tuesday, September 22nd, at The Westin DC Downtown and Howard University in Washington, DC.  This year’s theme is “Advancing Global Competitiveness: HBCUs Driving Innovation in AI, Intellectual Property, Emerging Technologies, and Strategic Industry–Government Partnerships.”</p>

<p> </p>

<p>The conference will be an innovative interactive experience as we bring together the Council of Engineering Deans of the Historically Black Colleges and Universities, students, engineering professionals, and leaders from top corporations and government agencies.  The AMIE Annual Conference will also feature prominent speakers and inspiring panel discussions. </p>

<p> </p>

<p>Why Attend?</p>

<p>Attendees will connect with HBCU leaders, researchers, and institutional partners who are advancing toward higher research activity, expanding industry-university collaboration, and building scalable pathways into high-demand fields. The conference offers a strategic setting to identify partnerships that align with federal and industry priorities, strengthen institutional capacity, and support long-term innovation outcomes.</p>

<p>Learn how HBCUs are expanding their research footprint and industry engagement.Explore partnership models aligned with federal, government, and corporate priorities.Meet leaders advancing innovation in the six critical technology areas: artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, quantum science, microelectronics and semiconductors, advanced manufacturing, and biotechnology. Identify collaboration opportunities that support both institutional growth and national needs.See how strategic partnerships with HBCUs can deliver measurable impact in talent recruitment and innovation. Gain early access to exceptional and innovative engineering and computer science talent and strengthen your recruitment talent pipeline.Conference Attire: Business Casual</p>

<p>Gala Attire: Business, Black Tie or Cocktail</p>

